# ── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── Secrets & keys — NEVER commit (these live on the host only) ───────────
*.sec
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
secring*
# SD-JWT runtime artifacts. Disclosures carry HOLDER CLAIMS — names, dates of
# birth, account identifiers — so the exposure is PII, not key material: none of
# the patterns above match a `sdjwt.json`, and gitleaks looks for credentials and
# has no opinion about a birthdate. The blanket pattern was removed in bd49b4d
# because, having no slash, it also matched `internal/sdjwt/sdjwt.go` and blocked
# the source file. Narrowed rather than dropped — the negation exempts the source
# and keeps the guard.
sdjwt.*
!sdjwt.go

# ── ZK trusted-setup artifacts (regenerate with cmd/zk-setup; large) ──────
*.pk
*.vk
*.ccs
zk/

# ── Crash dumps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.core

# ── Go build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/tr-svc
/spt-poc
/x402gate
/bin/
*.test

# ── Compiled command/client binaries — never commit (embed build paths) ───
clients/hcs-anchor/hcs-anchor
clients/hcs-anchor/spt-txn-hcs-anchor

